# Keep documentation current

After **any** feature, fix, rename, platform change, or new behavior, update **all** user-facing and developer docs in the same turn. Do not leave docs for “later”.

## Files that must stay in sync

| File | Language | Role |
|------|----------|------|
| `README.md` | EN | Product README (main) |
| `README.ru.md` | RU | Same content as EN README |
| `docs/TECHNICAL.md` | EN | Full technical doc (canonical) |
| `docs/TECHNICAL.ru.md` | RU | Same facts as EN TECHNICAL |
| `docs/DEVELOPER.md` | EN/short | iOS cheatsheet; must not contradict TECHNICAL |

EN and RU pairs must match on facts (bundle IDs, commands, languages, contacts, APIs). If you change one, change the other.

## What to update when

- **Identity** (name, bundle IDs, contacts, GitHub): README EN+RU + TECHNICAL EN+RU + DEVELOPER.
- **How to run / iOS / Android / signing**: README + TECHNICAL §14–18 + DEVELOPER.
- **API, login, 2FA, cache, languages, removed features**: TECHNICAL EN+RU (honesty table if completeness changed).
- **User-visible features**: README feature list EN+RU.

## Honesty

Document what the code actually does. If something is untested (e.g. live ELTE login), say so.

## End of task

Before finishing a change, scan the five files above for stale IDs, commands, or claims. Cross-link EN ↔ RU where a new doc is added.
